			"notes": "- Thirty-three fish. Vanilla still decides cod, salmon, pufferfish or tropical fish; the water decides which one.\n- Rivers, lakes, swamps, the sea and caves each have their own fish, and so do cold and warm water, the hour, the weather and the depth.\n- Every fish moves the way its family does, with a twist of its own, and fights as hard as a cod.\n- A tropical fish is named for what it is: a Clownfish, a Moorish Idol, a Lime-Gray Snooper.\n- Fish in the world are the same fish, and look it. Ponds, swamps and jungle rivers now have fish in them.\n- A landed fish is held up in front of you for a moment before it goes in the bag.\n- An Angler's Log advancement tab, for catching one of each.\n- With Village Quests, the fisherman teaches two new lessons: where the fish are, and how kin move alike."
		},
